---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Contact SympleHost"
  description="How to reach SympleHost support, partners, and the knowledge base team."
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <h1>Contact SympleHost</h1>
    <p>
      Use the channels below when you need help with your SympleHost workspace, Partner API access, or
      documentation on this knowledge base. We respond in English; Japanese and Indonesian support is
      available for common product questions through localized articles and the in-app experience.
    </p>
    <h2>Customer support</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:support@symplehost.ai">support@symplehost.ai</a> for account setup,
      channel connections, messaging automation, pricing, operations, billing questions, and bug
      reports. Include your workspace name, listing or reservation identifiers when relevant, and
      steps to reproduce so we can investigate faster.
    </p>
    <h2>Partners and API</h2>
    <p>
      For Partner API access, integration design, and commercial partnership inquiries, email
      <a href="mailto:partners@symplehost.ai">partners@symplehost.ai</a>. Technical reference lives at
      <a href="/partner-api.html">/partner-api.html</a> and
      <a href="/partner-api/openapi.yaml">/partner-api/openapi.yaml</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Documentation feedback</h2>
    <p>
      If an article is outdated, unclear, or missing a step, write to
      <a href="mailto:support@symplehost.ai">support@symplehost.ai</a> with the page URL and what you
      expected. Agents can also orient from <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> and the
      <a href="/sitemap-index.xml">sitemap</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Postal contact</h2>
    <p>
      SympleHost<br />
      Singapore<br />
      (Online product — primary contact is email)
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose-page { max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  .prose-page h1 { font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--heading-color); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .prose-page h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--heading-color); margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .prose-page p, .prose-page li { color: var(--foreground); line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 0.85rem; }
  .prose-page a { color: var(--primary); }
</style>
